meta {
  name: My tickets
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_tickets?scope=open&project=PROJ-0029&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  scope: open
  project: PROJ-0029
  limit: 20
  ~offset: 
  ~search: 
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
  
  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has has_more beside message", function () {
    expect(res.body.has_more).to.be.a("boolean");
  });

  test("rows have created, module and project_title", function () {
    if (res.body.message.length) {
      expect(res.body.message[0]).to.include.keys("created", "module", "project_title");
    }
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists the client's tickets, with filters and paging.
  
  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_tickets`  
  **Screen:** My Tickets
  
  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.
  
  **Query parameters:**
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `scope` | open / closed / all | no | `open` |  |
  | `project` | string | no | `PROJ-0029` |  |
  | `search` | string | no |  |  |
  | `limit` | int | no | `20` |  |
  | `offset` | int | no | `0` |  |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Client company. Send only when `me.customers` has more than one entry. Disabled by default. |
  
  **Response (trimmed):**
  
  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "12hnuea73s", "subject": "...", "status": "Resolved",
        "project": "PROJ-0029", "project_title": "Hamza ERPNext Implementation", "project_kind": "Implementation",
        "module": "Stock", "ticket_type": "Bug", "priority": "Normal",
        "created": "2026-10-28 15:41:40.112233", "needs_you": true
      }
    ],
    "has_more": false
  }
  ```

  - `has_more` sits beside `message`, not inside it. `true` = ask for the next page (`offset + limit`); `false` = this is the last page.
  - `created` is the raise date (same key as `get_ticket`). `creation` is also still sent for older app builds.
  
  **Errors:**
  
  - **401:** Token missing, expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403:** Not this client's record, or role not allowed.
  
  **Notes:**
  
  - Labels: New → Submitted, Triaged → Under review, In Progress → In progress (blue); Waiting on Client → Waiting on you (amber); Resolved → Ready for your testing (maroon); Closed (green).
  - `name` is a short random code: show it small and grey, lead with `subject`.
}
